### **KTH5702 series**

###### **Low power, high accuracy 2D Hall rotary position sensor**

**0x1Dh:**

|Bit Name|Bit|R/W|Decription|
|---|---|---|---|
|**measTime**|5:0|RW|During Continuous Sensing Mode and Wake-up & Sleep Mode, control the<br>intermittent waiting time between each measurement (standby state duration).<br>The value set in measTime controls the number of delays, with one lsb<br>corresponding to a waiting delay of 20 ms. The value in measTime corresponds to<br>the decimal setting and how many times the delay is performed.<br>If measTime = 0x05, the waiting time between the two measurements of the chip<br>is 5 times with a delay of 20ms, 5*20ms=100ms.|
|**measSel**|9:6|RW|Measure the select communication signal, when the host sends three<br>measurement mode commands to the chip without gating, can be gated by<br>measSel corresponding to the BA bit, i.e. measSel[3:0] = 0x06, then gate BA two<br>measurement channels.|
